      <!-- Section 5: Common Rejection Causes -->
      <h2>Common Reasons for Image Rejection on NTA and NBEMS Portals</h2>
      <ul class="rejection-list">
        <li><strong>Face Coverage Less Than 80%:</strong> Taking photos from too far away where the head and shoulders occupy less than 80% of the frame is the #1 reason for NTA rejection.</li>
        <li><strong>Signatures in Capital / Block Letters:</strong> Writing your name in uppercase letters or initials invalidates the signature according to official exam bulletins.</li>
        <li><strong>Faint or Blurry Signatures:</strong> Scanned signatures on shadowed, wrinkled, or ruled notebook paper fail automatic contrast validation. Always sign with dark ink on plain white unruled paper.</li>
        <li><strong>Colored or Outdoor Backgrounds:</strong> Backgrounds featuring blue curtains, trees, doors, or uneven shadows are strictly rejected. Only pure white backgrounds (#FFFFFF) are accepted.</li>
        <li><strong>Caps, Hats, or Dark Sunglasses:</strong> Headgear (except for mandatory religious attire) and tinted lenses are not permitted. Eyes and ears must be fully visible.</li>
      </ul>

